# The First Echo

Long ago, when the world was newly formed, a young spirit named Aria possessed the most beautiful voice in all creation. She sang to the mountains, the rivers, and the sky, filling the world with melodies that made flowers bloom and stars shine brighter.

But Aria was lonely. Her songs traveled far and wide, yet no voice ever sang back to her. The mountains stood silent, the rivers only gurgled, and the wind merely whistled without words.

One day, heartbroken by the silence, Aria climbed the highest mountain and sang her saddest song. She poured all her loneliness into the melody, her voice trembling with emotion. When she finished, she wept.

Then something miraculous happened. The mountain sang back to her—not with its own voice, but with hers. The cliffs and caves had caught her song and returned it, softer and more distant, but unmistakably her own melody.

Aria's tears turned to joy. She sang again, and again the mountain replied. She laughed, and heard her laughter return.

From that day forward, Aria traveled to every canyon and cave, leaving pieces of her voice behind so that no one would ever sing alone again. This is why, even now, when you call out to the mountains, they always call back.
